{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n1. **Presentation uses the returned value's `format`.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` sets a custom formatter that produces \"formatted input: source\" and asserts that text is in the user message.\n   - `fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` checks that the domain's contents reach the agent in order.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` checks the rendered contents of queued inputs.\n   - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` shows `format` uses the retained value.\n\n2. **Text and fingerprint describe the same observation.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` changes the underlying content after the read. It asserts `format()` still returns \"before\", the fingerprint is unchanged, and there was only one read.\n   - The agent tests above assert that the recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprint matches the presented content, with a single read per input.\n\n3. **Queued ask-builder failures return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n   - `validation_tests.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` covers a loading failure (`fail_read`, giving `Graph(\"read\")`) and a preparation failure (`fail_prepare`, giving `Graph(\"render\")`).\n   - It also asserts that no agent request is made and no dependency is recorded.\n\n4. **A `read_node` tool call returns the failure as a tool error so the agent can recover.**\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` has the domain's `node_content` fail.\n   - It asserts a `read_node` tool result with `is_error`, the exact error text, a second request in which the agent continues and submits, and no recorded dependencies.\n   - Loading and preparation both happen inside `Domain::node_content`, so a failure from either takes the same path.\n\nI found no gaps, marking gaps or unacknowledged omissions.",
  "references": "2f91eb887272d526f4a252d54e6afbef9806450ccce1db796d72de96bb1e8334",
